  "veld": "Write .veld contracts once; generate typed servers and clients.\nVeld only ever writes inside a target's `out` directory and never touches your own files.\n\nUsage: veld [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  init      Create veld.toml and an example contract\n  check     Compile all contracts, lint them and report diagnostics\n  generate  Generate code for every target (or one, by name)\n  clean     Remove generated files that you have not modified\n  setup     Wire generated targets into your apps (package.json, pom.xml, build.gradle)\n  doctor    Check the project, its tools and its environment, and say how to fix problems\n  fmt       Format .veld files canonically\n  diff      Show breaking and non-breaking contract changes\n  test      Run the `example` blocks of the contracts, offline or against a live test handler\n  export    Export OpenAPI or the compiled IR\n  plugin    Create and test emitter plugins\n  add       Add a registry package to veld.toml, resolve it and pin it in veld.lock\n  install   Install exactly the packages pinned in veld.lock\n  publish   Pack this project's library or service and upload it to the registry\n  login     Store a registry API token\n  logout    Forget the stored registry token\n  registry  Look things up in the registry: info, search, versions, token\n  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --config <PATH>\n          Path to veld.toml (or a directory containing it). Default: search upward from here\n\n  -q, --quiet\n          Print only errors and warnings\n\n      --no-color\n          Never colour output\n\n  -v, --verbose...\n          Show phases, write-plan entries and timings (repeat for more detail)\n\n  -h, --help\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')\n\n  -V, --version\n          Print version",
  "veld init": "Create veld.toml and an example contract\n\nUsage: veld init [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --config <PATH>\n          Path to veld.toml (or a directory containing it). Default: search upward from here\n\n      --name <NAME>\n          Project name (default: the directory name)\n\n  -q, --quiet\n          Print only errors and warnings\n\n      --workspace [<SERVICES>]\n          Scaffold a microservices workspace; optionally the comma-separated service names\n\n      --no-color\n          Never colour output\n\n      --server <KIND[:FRAMEWORK]>\n          Server target: node[:express|fastify|hono|nest|node-http], java[:jdk|spring], rust[:axum] or none. Prefix with `service=` to set one service of a workspace\n\n      --client <KIND[:FRAMEWORK]>\n          Client targets (repeat or comma-separate): typescript[:react|vue], java, rust[:reqwest|ureq] or none\n\n  -v, --verbose...\n          Show phases, write-plan entries and timings (repeat for more detail)\n\n      --base-url <SERVICE=URL>\n          Base URL of a workspace service, as SERVICE=URL (repeatable; default http://localhost:300N)\n\n      --consumes <SERVICE=A,B>\n          Services a workspace service consumes, as SERVICE=a,b (repeatable; nothing is consumed by default)\n\n      --out <TARGET=DIR>\n          Change the output folder of a target, as TARGET=DIR (repeatable)\n\n      --description <TEXT>\n          A one-line project description, written to veld.toml\n\n  -y, --yes\n          Use the defaults for everything not given as a flag; never prompt\n\n      --dry-run\n          List the files that would be written, and write nothing\n\n      --template <NAME>\n          Starter contracts: `hello` (default) or `crud` (users, auth and pagination)\n\n          Possible values:\n          - hello: One tiny service with a `hello` endpoint\n          - crud:  Users CRUD, auth (login, token) and a reusable `Page` type\n\n  -h, --help\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')",
  "veld check": "Compile all contracts, lint them and report diagnostics\n\nUsage: veld check [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...\n\nArguments:\n  [PATHS]...  Report only diagnostics in these .veld files or directories (the project still compiles whole)\n\nOptions:\n      --config <PATH>            Path to veld.toml (or a directory containing it). Default: search upward from here\n      --no-lint                  Skip the lint rules\n  -q, --quiet                    Print only errors and warnings\n      --strict                   Lint warnings fail the check too\n      --graph [<FORMAT>]         Print the service dependency graph instead of the summary [possible values: text, dot, json]\n      --no-color                 Never colour output\n      --prove                    Ask an external SMT solver about the rules: for `check`, whether they contradict each other; for `diff`, whether a changed rule got tighter\n  -v, --verbose...               Show phases, write-plan entries and timings (repeat for more detail)\n      --solver <PATH>            With --prove: the solver program (default: VELD_SOLVER, then z3 and cvc5 on PATH)\n      --prove-timeout <SECONDS>  With --prove: the time limit of each question, in seconds (default: 5)\n  -h, --help                     Print help",
